1
00:00:00,059 --> 00:00:01,059
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:01,059 --> 00:00:02,059
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:02,059 --> 00:00:03,659
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:03,659 --> 00:00:07,199
[Episode 13]

5
00:00:07,199 --> 00:00:10,347
Even if it's difficult, make sure
you stretch at home every day.

6
00:00:10,347 --> 00:00:14,215
Take your medication twice a day,
and I'll see you again in a week.

7
00:00:14,215 --> 00:00:15,743
Yes, Doctor. Thank you.

8
00:00:15,743 --> 00:00:17,443
Take care.

9
00:00:20,715 --> 00:00:23,911
Dr. Oh, that was your last patient.

10
00:00:23,911 --> 00:00:25,671
You worked hard today.

11
00:00:25,671 --> 00:00:28,491
Goodness, I didn't realize it was this late.

12
00:00:28,491 --> 00:00:30,792
You did a great job too, Ms. Jung.

13
00:00:32,943 --> 00:00:34,643
Jeez.

14
00:00:42,192 --> 00:00:43,926
[Oh Seong Nam Orthopedic Clinic,
Director Oh Seong Nam]

15
00:00:55,755 --> 00:00:57,995
[Do Not Enter, Investigation in Progress]

16
00:00:59,003 --> 00:01:00,135
Ugh.

17
00:01:00,135 --> 00:01:02,259
They shot him in the eye again.
What's the deal?

18
00:01:02,259 --> 00:01:03,492
Did the bullet just happen to hit his eye?

19
00:01:03,492 --> 00:01:05,243
Or was it intentional?

20
00:01:05,243 --> 00:01:08,187
Twice in a row?
Then it had to be intentional.

21
00:01:08,187 --> 00:01:11,303
Last time, the left eye. Today, the right.

22
00:01:11,303 --> 00:01:13,399
Wow. That's insane.

23
00:01:13,399 --> 00:01:15,787
Why would they do this when they
never even did it to the worst criminals...

24
00:01:15,787 --> 00:01:18,275
Are you sure you found nothing?

25
00:01:18,275 --> 00:01:20,371
Yeah. Nothing again.

26
00:01:20,371 --> 00:01:23,983
At most, he had a traffic fine
for running a light seven years ago.

27
00:01:23,983 --> 00:01:26,647
Anyway, is Kingfisher
seriously insane or what?

28
00:01:26,647 --> 00:01:29,926
Why would he suddenly start killing people
who aren't even criminals?

29
00:01:35,847 --> 00:01:39,939
Wow, it's completely open outside.
Where on earth did the shot come from?

30
00:01:39,939 --> 00:01:42,526
Unless he flew through the air
to take the shot,

31
00:01:43,415 --> 00:01:44,974
he must've fired from across the river.

32
00:01:44,974 --> 00:01:46,551
No way!

33
00:01:46,551 --> 00:01:49,326
From all the way over there?
Is that even possible?

34
00:02:14,003 --> 00:02:17,611
<i>Another shooting has taken place
following last weekend's incident.</i>

35
00:02:17,611 --> 00:02:19,067
[Another Fatal Shooting, Doctor in His 40s]
<i>The latest victim</i>

36
00:02:19,067 --> 00:02:21,187
[Shot Dead in Hospital Office]
<i>was a practicing doctor in his late 40s,</i>

37
00:02:21,187 --> 00:02:24,459
<i>who was killed
late yesterday afternoon in his clinic</i>

38
00:02:24,459 --> 00:02:26,843
[Good Deed Award, Oh Seong Nam]
<i>by a bullet that penetrated the window.</i>

39
00:02:26,843 --> 00:02:28,675
<i>He was pronounced dead at the scene.</i>

40
00:02:28,675 --> 00:02:31,811
<i>Just three days ago, a middle school teacher
in his 50s was shot dead</i>

41
00:02:31,811 --> 00:02:35,559
<i>while crossing a crosswalk
in broad daylight in the heart of the city.</i>

42
00:02:35,559 --> 00:02:38,467
<i>Now, another civilian
has been killed by gunfire,</i>

43
00:02:38,467 --> 00:02:40,903
<i>sending shockwaves across the country.</i>

44
00:02:40,903 --> 00:02:42,323
[Kingfisher Only Targeted Criminals]
<i>As this is the first time Kingfisher,</i>

45
00:02:42,323 --> 00:02:43,991
[Why Kill Innocent Civilians?]
<i>which has only targeted criminals,</i>

46
00:02:43,991 --> 00:02:46,903
[Hero or Murderer?]
<i>has gone after ordinary citizens,</i>

47
00:02:46,903 --> 00:02:48,682
[Public Opinion Turns After Civilian Deaths]
<i>investigators are also looking closely</i>

48
00:02:48,682 --> 00:02:52,583
<i>into the identities of the two victims
and any connection between them.</i>

49
00:02:52,583 --> 00:02:54,392
Who could have...

50
00:03:07,051 --> 00:03:11,435
Honey, I think Yul wants to show
her friends that she went to Jeju Island.

51
00:03:11,435 --> 00:03:12,647
Let's show Daddy.

52
00:03:12,647 --> 00:03:14,347
Ta-da!

53
00:03:15,847 --> 00:03:18,747
Did you have that much fun
going on a trip with Mommy and Daddy?

54
00:03:18,747 --> 00:03:21,959
Yeah, it was so much fun.

55
00:03:21,959 --> 00:03:25,175
Yul, show this to your friends,
and then put it in your bag, okay?

56
00:03:25,175 --> 00:03:26,792
- Okay.
- Okay.

57
00:03:26,792 --> 00:03:29,075
Come on, put it on.

58
00:03:29,075 --> 00:03:32,831
Come on, let's go! Tangerine Girl.

59
00:03:32,831 --> 00:03:34,531
Let's go!

60
00:03:35,926 --> 00:03:37,171
[Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency]

61
00:03:37,171 --> 00:03:40,971
As previously reported,
neither victim had a criminal record,

62
00:03:40,971 --> 00:03:44,426
and no other criminal activity
has been identified.

63
00:03:45,303 --> 00:03:47,519
Is there no connection
between the two victims?

64
00:03:47,519 --> 00:03:51,231
No. At this point, we haven't found
any connection between them.

65
00:03:51,231 --> 00:03:54,619
They have no overlap in hometowns,
schools, occupations, neighborhoods,

66
00:03:54,619 --> 00:03:57,126
or periods of military service.

67
00:03:58,255 --> 00:04:00,559
Have you identified the sniper locations?

68
00:04:01,783 --> 00:04:05,027
The first sniper location was
a building under construction.

69
00:04:05,027 --> 00:04:08,067
There were no CCTV cameras inside,
and the area outside has heavy foot traffic,

70
00:04:08,067 --> 00:04:10,791
making it difficult to identify a suspect.

71
00:04:10,791 --> 00:04:16,139
The second shot was fired from about
two kilometers across the Han River.

72
00:04:16,139 --> 00:04:18,072
Our forensic team
is currently tracking the shooter

73
00:04:18,072 --> 00:04:20,226
based on evidence from the scene.

74
00:04:24,175 --> 00:04:26,835
Isn't it possible that
the shooter isn't Kingfisher?

75
00:04:26,835 --> 00:04:29,259
A copycat, for instance.

76
00:04:35,859 --> 00:04:38,635
Both cases clearly bear similarities
to the previous attacks:

77
00:04:38,635 --> 00:04:43,887
long-range shots, a single bullet,
and the location of the gunshot wound.

78
00:04:43,887 --> 00:04:46,571
But isn't the most important
difference the targets?

79
00:04:46,571 --> 00:04:48,159
In the past 15 years,

80
00:04:48,159 --> 00:04:51,299
Kingfisher has never once
harmed an innocent civilian.

81
00:04:51,299 --> 00:04:53,867
Well, the nature of a crime
can change at any time.

82
00:04:53,867 --> 00:04:56,692
What matters is the method.

83
00:04:58,843 --> 00:05:02,831
Our task force considers Kingfisher
the prime suspect in both cases,

84
00:05:02,831 --> 00:05:04,943
no, in fact, effectively the only suspect,

85
00:05:04,943 --> 00:05:06,892
and we will do everything
we can to apprehend him.

86
00:05:06,892 --> 00:05:07,892
That's all.

87
00:05:07,892 --> 00:05:11,292
[Sniper locations]

88
00:05:22,339 --> 00:05:23,723
Ma'am,

89
00:05:23,723 --> 00:05:27,607
do you have any theory on why
he suddenly changed his targets?

90
00:05:27,607 --> 00:05:29,423
It's extremely rare for a serial killer

91
00:05:29,423 --> 00:05:32,143
like Kingfisher to suddenly
abandon his beliefs.

92
00:05:32,143 --> 00:05:36,426
Especially someone who's followed
such a consistent pattern for so long.

93
00:05:37,655 --> 00:05:40,392
If he's changed his targets, that means...

94
00:05:40,999 --> 00:05:43,726
the purpose behind the killings has changed.

95
00:05:45,595 --> 00:05:49,131
Well, let's wait and see
how the investigation develops.

96
00:05:49,131 --> 00:05:51,192
- Okay.
- Understood.

97
00:05:55,292 --> 00:05:56,635
[Reporter Kwon Tae Seong]

98
00:05:56,635 --> 00:05:58,659
- Oh, one moment, please.
- Yeah.

99
00:06:00,099 --> 00:06:01,799
Where are you?

100
00:06:04,383 --> 00:06:06,263
Doesn't he seem a little down lately?

101
00:06:06,263 --> 00:06:07,704
Kingfisher's someone
he has spent years hunting

102
00:06:07,704 --> 00:06:09,039
in principle as a police officer.

103
00:06:09,039 --> 00:06:12,259
He's spent a long time
studying him in the process.

104
00:06:12,259 --> 00:06:16,292
He couldn't condone it,
but thought the guy drew the line.

105
00:06:17,795 --> 00:06:20,526
Maybe it's a little disillusioning
to see that change?

106
00:06:25,766 --> 00:06:28,071
- What is it?
- A gift from Yul.

107
00:06:28,071 --> 00:06:29,771
A gift?

108
00:06:32,063 --> 00:06:34,231
You went to Jeju Island? When?

109
00:06:34,231 --> 00:06:36,931
Well... Last weekend, with my family.

110
00:06:38,715 --> 00:06:41,143
While some of us are working
our asses off without a single weekend off,

111
00:06:41,143 --> 00:06:43,092
you guys are out having fun.

112
00:06:44,299 --> 00:06:46,443
Yul's gift is so cute.

113
00:06:46,443 --> 00:06:47,487
So...

114
00:06:47,487 --> 00:06:52,095
While we were in Jeju Island,
Seoul was turned completely upside down.

115
00:06:52,095 --> 00:06:54,379
You must've been swamped, huh?

116
00:06:54,379 --> 00:06:58,095
You didn't bring a swamped person here
just to hand over this, right?

117
00:06:58,095 --> 00:07:03,159
You know I can't say anything
beyond the official briefing, right?

118
00:07:06,459 --> 00:07:10,259
Forget the official line.
What's your gut telling you?

119
00:07:12,471 --> 00:07:14,167
Hey.

120
00:07:14,167 --> 00:07:19,099
If there's another punk like Kingfisher
in this country, that's a tragedy.

121
00:07:19,099 --> 00:07:21,126
That's your conclusion?

122
00:07:25,975 --> 00:07:29,863
I think you have a different opinion.

123
00:07:29,863 --> 00:07:32,247
You told me once before.

124
00:07:32,247 --> 00:07:36,063
You said, "Who knows when that gun
might be turned on an innocent person?"

125
00:07:36,063 --> 00:07:38,092
Do you still think that?

126
00:07:39,687 --> 00:07:42,363
What if someone killed them
out of personal revenge

127
00:07:42,363 --> 00:07:45,291
and framed Kingfisher for it?

128
00:07:45,291 --> 00:07:48,592
Is that your conclusion?

129
00:07:50,691 --> 00:07:52,391
Wow.

130
00:07:55,391 --> 00:07:59,639
Why do I feel like
you're defending Kingfisher?

131
00:07:59,639 --> 00:08:02,071
The same punk who threatened you, no less.

132
00:08:02,071 --> 00:08:03,219
If he were the kind of punk
who'd kill anyone,

133
00:08:03,219 --> 00:08:05,959
he would've killed me
instead of threatening me back then.

134
00:08:07,295 --> 00:08:09,643
Got any proof?

135
00:08:09,643 --> 00:08:12,359
Proof that Kingfisher was framed.

136
00:08:14,983 --> 00:08:17,026
That's what I'm going to find out now.

137
00:08:18,355 --> 00:08:21,659
You do your job. I'll do mine.

138
00:08:22,395 --> 00:08:24,095
I'm out.

139
00:08:29,615 --> 00:08:31,192
<i>I knew that punk
would cross the line someday.</i>

140
00:08:31,192 --> 00:08:32,995
<i>He's finally shown his true colors.</i>

141
00:08:32,995 --> 00:08:35,326
<i>A hero who catches criminals?
What a show-off.</i>

142
00:08:35,326 --> 00:08:37,107
- <i>He's the criminal himself.</i>
- <i>True justice?</i>

143
00:08:37,107 --> 00:08:38,795
<i>Catching Kingfisher is justice.</i>

144
00:08:38,795 --> 00:08:40,715
<i>How are we supposed to live like this,
wondering when we'll get shot?</i>

145
00:08:40,715 --> 00:08:42,267
<i>What on earth are the police doing?
Why haven't they caught him yet?</i>

146
00:08:42,267 --> 00:08:44,559
People's views have totally changed.

147
00:08:44,559 --> 00:08:46,209
The comments are all hate too.

148
00:08:46,209 --> 00:08:48,611
These people...

149
00:08:48,611 --> 00:08:50,992
How dare they compare
a fake to the real deal?

150
00:08:52,723 --> 00:08:55,847
Taking someone out with a single shot
from that distance and angle

151
00:08:55,847 --> 00:08:58,392
means he's a professional,
probably on Director Yoo's level.

152
00:08:58,392 --> 00:09:01,526
He's clearly someone who has no qualms

153
00:09:01,526 --> 00:09:05,703
about sacrificing innocent people
to achieve his goal.

154
00:09:05,703 --> 00:09:08,491
What exactly is the point of all this?

155
00:09:08,491 --> 00:09:11,192
Kingfisher's social death?

156
00:09:17,631 --> 00:09:23,326
Instead of attacking me directly,
they're going after public opinion?

157
00:09:25,483 --> 00:09:28,026
If the goal is to turn
Kingfisher into a villain,

158
00:09:28,026 --> 00:09:30,026
two victims won't be enough.

159
00:09:30,026 --> 00:09:32,919
The more victims there are,
the greater the impact.

160
00:09:32,919 --> 00:09:36,326
We have to catch him
before there's a third victim.

161
00:09:36,326 --> 00:09:39,467
Ki Yeong Do,
did you look into what I asked for?

162
00:09:39,467 --> 00:09:41,583
It's ready.

163
00:09:41,583 --> 00:09:43,535
Here's the CCTV footage from the first case.

164
00:09:43,535 --> 00:09:46,759
This was taken just before the shooting.

165
00:09:46,759 --> 00:09:50,779
What's with that disabled man all bundled up?

166
00:09:50,779 --> 00:09:53,319
Isn't he hot in the middle of summer?

167
00:09:53,319 --> 00:09:55,471
Could he be deliberately hiding his face?

168
00:09:55,471 --> 00:09:59,475
Looks like the victim
approached him first to offer help.

169
00:09:59,475 --> 00:10:03,375
The victim had volunteered
with a disability organization before.

170
00:10:03,375 --> 00:10:08,327
He could've used that to lure
the victim to the sniper location.

171
00:10:08,327 --> 00:10:10,335
Your hunch was right.

172
00:10:10,335 --> 00:10:13,947
This is CCTV footage from outside
the hospital that morning.

173
00:10:13,947 --> 00:10:14,947
Oh, look!

174
00:10:14,947 --> 00:10:17,339
There's that man in the wheelchair again.

175
00:10:17,339 --> 00:10:19,075
Why would he go there?

176
00:10:19,075 --> 00:10:21,843
It doesn't look like he had
any particular role that day.

177
00:10:21,843 --> 00:10:23,592
"Catch me if you can."

178
00:10:32,443 --> 00:10:35,292
He's leaving us a trail to follow.

179
00:10:37,692 --> 00:10:39,611
All right. Let's follow it.

180
00:10:39,611 --> 00:10:43,579
Yeah. If we follow it, we'll eventually
find the killer's trail too.

181
00:10:43,579 --> 00:10:46,343
We have to find him
before there's another victim.

182
00:10:46,343 --> 00:10:47,719
You can do it, right?

183
00:10:47,719 --> 00:10:49,659
Yes, understood.

184
00:10:57,259 --> 00:11:00,271
We can't get into the scene.

185
00:11:00,271 --> 00:11:03,591
The hospital's probably closed anyway.

186
00:11:03,591 --> 00:11:05,843
Forget the scene.

187
00:11:05,843 --> 00:11:07,659
Let's start over there.

188
00:11:07,659 --> 00:11:09,375
[Oh Seong Nam Orthopedic Clinic]
Where?

189
00:11:09,375 --> 00:11:13,587
Do you know anything about
Dr. Oh Seong Nam, the director here?

190
00:11:13,587 --> 00:11:14,992
Oh Seong Nam?

191
00:11:14,992 --> 00:11:18,692
I haven't really heard anything about him.

192
00:11:20,487 --> 00:11:22,435
[Oh Seong Nam, Orthopedic Surgeon]

193
00:11:23,811 --> 00:11:25,850
- That's the CCTV camera outside, right?
- Yes.

194
00:11:25,850 --> 00:11:29,535
Can we check three days
of footage around the incident?

195
00:11:29,535 --> 00:11:34,287
Have you noticed anyone suspicious
hanging around here lately?

196
00:11:34,287 --> 00:11:35,987
No.

197
00:11:36,871 --> 00:11:37,871
Here you go.

198
00:11:37,871 --> 00:11:40,959
- We'll make a copy and return it.
- Sure.

199
00:11:40,959 --> 00:11:42,691
[Copying]

200
00:11:42,691 --> 00:11:45,595
Mr. Lee, they found
the second sniper location.

201
00:11:45,595 --> 00:11:47,891
Thank you.

202
00:11:47,891 --> 00:11:48,951
- Let's go.
- Right.

203
00:11:48,951 --> 00:11:50,583
Dr. Oh Seong Nam.

204
00:11:50,583 --> 00:11:52,171
Oh, yes.

205
00:11:52,171 --> 00:11:56,771
Do you happen to remember
anyone who accompanied him?

206
00:11:56,771 --> 00:12:00,559
I'm not sure. Not really.

207
00:12:00,559 --> 00:12:05,355
Oh, I think they were mostly men
around his age.

208
00:12:05,355 --> 00:12:07,392
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

209
00:12:09,767 --> 00:12:13,611
Were they usually other doctors, then?

210
00:12:13,611 --> 00:12:16,551
Well, I'm not sure about that...

211
00:12:16,551 --> 00:12:17,983
Is this the place?

212
00:12:17,983 --> 00:12:19,907
Yes. Based on the trajectory calculations,

213
00:12:19,907 --> 00:12:22,759
this is the only location
within the margin of error.

214
00:12:28,879 --> 00:12:30,707
The building was completed a few months ago,

215
00:12:30,707 --> 00:12:32,959
but it's still vacant,
so the CCTV wasn't operational.

216
00:12:32,959 --> 00:12:35,959
Wow. I don't know how he
managed to pick a place like this.

217
00:12:43,663 --> 00:12:45,103
Oh, but this is really strange.

218
00:12:45,103 --> 00:12:47,255
What is?

219
00:12:47,255 --> 00:12:49,219
There were no working CCTV cameras
at the first scene either.

220
00:12:49,219 --> 00:12:53,063
Why pick places like this
instead of wiping the footage like before?

221
00:12:53,063 --> 00:12:55,339
Something about this
just doesn't feel like Kingfisher...

222
00:12:55,339 --> 00:12:57,426
And what exactly is "like Kingfisher"?

223
00:12:57,426 --> 00:12:58,895
What?

224
00:12:58,895 --> 00:13:01,343
I mean, starting with the fact
that he's killing innocent people...

225
00:13:01,343 --> 00:13:03,379
Whether he killed guilty people
or innocent people,

226
00:13:03,379 --> 00:13:05,419
he killed someone. We have to catch him.

227
00:13:05,419 --> 00:13:07,487
We just need to do our jobs.

228
00:13:07,487 --> 00:13:09,192
Okay.

229
00:13:10,215 --> 00:13:13,492
We'll know once we catch him
whether he's Kingfisher or not.

230
00:13:16,543 --> 00:13:20,083
Looks like hair was found here too.
There was some over there as well.

231
00:13:20,083 --> 00:13:22,859
Weren't the sniper locations usually clean?

232
00:13:29,899 --> 00:13:34,892
Darn it, who on earth has a death wish?

233
00:13:39,867 --> 00:13:43,939
Darn it, how do I catch this punk?

234
00:13:43,939 --> 00:13:46,992
Just wait till I get my hands on him.

235
00:13:53,771 --> 00:13:55,924
Manager Tae Min,
why are you just sitting there?

236
00:13:55,924 --> 00:13:57,892
You need to do something!

237
00:14:00,963 --> 00:14:04,031
Our Kingfisher is about
to be branded a murderer.

238
00:14:04,031 --> 00:14:05,627
Her reputation is in the gutter!

239
00:14:05,627 --> 00:14:07,231
You two have been friends
since you were kids.

240
00:14:07,231 --> 00:14:09,043
And you're just going to sit there
like it's nothing?

241
00:14:09,043 --> 00:14:12,427
His movement pattern
confirms he was near the crime scene,

242
00:14:12,427 --> 00:14:13,999
though not on the day itself,
but a day or two before.

243
00:14:13,999 --> 00:14:15,711
Oh, what's he saying?

244
00:14:15,711 --> 00:14:18,175
<i>Okay, I'm here.</i>

245
00:14:18,175 --> 00:14:20,467
[Yoo Bo Na]

246
00:14:20,467 --> 00:14:22,095
What are you doing?

247
00:14:22,095 --> 00:14:23,992
Room 1803.

248
00:14:25,931 --> 00:14:28,392
Calm Oh Hyun Nam down.

249
00:14:29,626 --> 00:14:30,826
I'll put the key to good use.

250
00:14:30,826 --> 00:14:32,559
[Yoo Bo Na]

251
00:14:37,491 --> 00:14:39,859
So you were doing something after all.

252
00:14:40,623 --> 00:14:42,426
You really are friends.

253
00:14:44,471 --> 00:14:47,092
But where did Director Yoo go?

254
00:14:48,807 --> 00:14:50,507
Huh?

255
00:15:24,659 --> 00:15:26,943
[Caller ID Restricted]

256
00:15:26,943 --> 00:15:30,375
<i>Surprise! Hi, my friend.</i>

257
00:15:30,375 --> 00:15:32,275
Changed your shoes?

258
00:15:32,275 --> 00:15:35,503
It's too hot to keep wearing those.

259
00:15:35,503 --> 00:15:38,899
Is there anything in the room?
Can you see me?

260
00:15:38,899 --> 00:15:40,351
Why ask?

261
00:15:40,351 --> 00:15:42,635
I know why you came.

262
00:15:42,635 --> 00:15:43,719
But it wasn't me.

263
00:15:43,719 --> 00:15:47,011
I know. The shooting was pretty precise.

264
00:15:47,011 --> 00:15:50,459
You're actually pretty lousy
at sniping, aren't you?

265
00:15:51,675 --> 00:15:53,643
Only because you're a monster.

266
00:15:53,643 --> 00:15:55,759
<i>I'm not exactly lousy, you know.</i>

267
00:15:56,451 --> 00:15:58,611
Did Mama send you?

268
00:15:58,611 --> 00:16:01,292
<i>Mama would be hurt to hear that.</i>

269
00:16:02,019 --> 00:16:03,351
Then who is it?

270
00:16:03,351 --> 00:16:09,523
Someone who can imitate Kingfisher
and wants to bring you down?

271
00:16:09,523 --> 00:16:11,223
<i>I'm busy.</i>

272
00:16:16,919 --> 00:16:19,926
I told you that you'd be the one
to come looking for me first.

273
00:17:16,219 --> 00:17:18,826
Seriously, these monsters...

274
00:17:20,403 --> 00:17:23,739
Yoo Bo Na better watch her back.

275
00:17:23,739 --> 00:17:25,739
[Funeral Hall]
Oh, these people just won't listen.

276
00:17:25,739 --> 00:17:28,103
Get out, seriously!

277
00:17:28,103 --> 00:17:31,839
If you come in here one more time,
I'm calling the police.

278
00:17:31,839 --> 00:17:33,787
Unbelievable, jeez...

279
00:17:33,787 --> 00:17:35,487
Go on in.

280
00:17:38,771 --> 00:17:42,703
In the end, we got kicked out
without even speaking to the family.

281
00:17:42,703 --> 00:17:44,079
At least we paid our respects.

282
00:17:44,079 --> 00:17:46,679
And we got a feel for the atmosphere inside.

283
00:17:46,679 --> 00:17:51,459
What, should we camp out at the entrance too?

284
00:17:55,107 --> 00:17:56,967
<i>They found Kingfisher's
second sniper location.</i>

285
00:17:56,967 --> 00:18:00,643
<i>Head over there. See if you can find
anything at the scene. Anything at all.</i>

286
00:18:00,643 --> 00:18:01,971
That was the Chief.

287
00:18:01,971 --> 00:18:05,099
He wants us to check if they found
anything at the second sniper location.

288
00:18:05,099 --> 00:18:09,951
The reporters camped out there
can cover it themselves.

289
00:18:09,951 --> 00:18:13,751
Let the police handle the shooter.
We'll look into the victims.

290
00:18:13,751 --> 00:18:16,592
Let's check out the first victim tomorrow.

291
00:18:16,592 --> 00:18:17,592
- Okay, sir.
- Well...

292
00:18:17,592 --> 00:18:19,826
He was an upstanding, law-abiding man.

293
00:18:19,826 --> 00:18:22,327
He was kind to his patients.

294
00:18:22,327 --> 00:18:24,667
He must have been
a real family man at home too.

295
00:18:24,667 --> 00:18:26,826
He traveled abroad every year.

296
00:18:26,826 --> 00:18:31,699
He went to Cambodia last year
and was planning to go to Bali this year.

297
00:18:31,699 --> 00:18:35,243
Why would anyone kill a man like that?
That darn Kingfisher.

298
00:18:35,243 --> 00:18:37,359
Jeez, what a punk.

299
00:18:38,991 --> 00:18:41,611
Not long ago they worshiped him as a hero,

300
00:18:41,611 --> 00:18:45,326
and now they treat him
like public enemy number one.

301
00:19:14,792 --> 00:19:16,635
[Tae Seong Chicken]

302
00:19:16,635 --> 00:19:18,335
Ms. Se Ah?

303
00:19:36,992 --> 00:19:38,215
[Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency]

304
00:19:38,215 --> 00:19:41,026
Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency?

305
00:19:41,759 --> 00:19:44,126
[Going All the Way This Time,
Kingfisher Task Force Launched]

306
00:19:44,126 --> 00:19:46,126
[Past Cases Under Review
with New Investigative Techniques]

307
00:19:59,195 --> 00:20:01,407
What is this?

308
00:20:01,407 --> 00:20:03,026
Wait, don't tell me you made this yourself...

309
00:20:03,026 --> 00:20:05,643
No, Sun Il did.

310
00:20:05,643 --> 00:20:08,967
I'm telling you again, I didn't make it.

311
00:20:08,967 --> 00:20:13,292
Sun Il made it to thank you
for boosting sales.

312
00:20:14,199 --> 00:20:15,683
Who cares who made it?

313
00:20:15,683 --> 00:20:18,043
Oh, I was craving something
spicy anyway. This is great.

314
00:20:18,043 --> 00:20:19,515
I'll have to order more often.

315
00:20:19,515 --> 00:20:21,887
You really want to get deep-fried
instead of the chicken, huh?

316
00:20:21,887 --> 00:20:24,747
Why would someone craving
something spicy order chicken?

317
00:20:24,747 --> 00:20:26,383
I nearly died getting all the way here.

318
00:20:26,383 --> 00:20:28,215
Yum!

319
00:20:28,215 --> 00:20:29,231
Is it good?

320
00:20:29,231 --> 00:20:30,931
Yeah.

321
00:20:34,467 --> 00:20:35,607
So...

322
00:20:35,607 --> 00:20:37,895
is police work...

323
00:20:37,895 --> 00:20:40,292
really tough?

324
00:20:41,695 --> 00:20:43,591
Are you worried about me?

325
00:20:43,591 --> 00:20:44,959
Yeah.

326
00:20:44,959 --> 00:20:46,459
As if. You want to die?

327
00:20:46,459 --> 00:20:48,883
Yes or no? Just give me the facts.

328
00:20:48,883 --> 00:20:50,859
"Yes or no? Just give me the facts..."

329
00:20:55,611 --> 00:20:56,811
Huh?

330
00:20:56,811 --> 00:20:58,887
Assistant Manager Ki, what brings you here?

331
00:20:58,887 --> 00:21:02,155
Oh, well, you see.
I wasn't going from here to there.

332
00:21:02,155 --> 00:21:04,819
But I was going from there to here,
and then I saw the convenience store.

333
00:21:04,819 --> 00:21:06,907
I'm really thirsty.
They sell bottled water, right?

334
00:21:06,907 --> 00:21:09,026
Yes, they do. I suppose so.

335
00:21:14,891 --> 00:21:16,992
He came to the convenience store.

336
00:21:25,879 --> 00:21:26,947
Good to see you again.

337
00:21:26,947 --> 00:21:28,647
Indeed.

338
00:21:29,295 --> 00:21:32,926
You seem to really enjoy
butting into other people's business, huh?

339
00:21:33,591 --> 00:21:35,659
But I didn't butt in this time.

340
00:21:39,675 --> 00:21:41,731
You seem to be working yourself to the bone.

341
00:21:41,731 --> 00:21:44,739
Well, do you at least get overtime pay?

342
00:21:44,739 --> 00:21:48,947
Looks like you didn't even wash your hair.
Public service must be taking a toll.

343
00:21:48,947 --> 00:21:51,159
Don't they even let you eat?

344
00:21:51,903 --> 00:21:54,203
I save time by skipping meals.

345
00:21:54,203 --> 00:21:56,247
We're after a very hot target these days.

346
00:21:56,247 --> 00:21:58,379
I hope you're not chasing the wrong shadow.

347
00:21:58,379 --> 00:21:59,651
And who do you think I'm talking about?

348
00:21:59,651 --> 00:22:02,426
The whole world is buzzing about him.

349
00:22:05,427 --> 00:22:07,607
You don't think it's Kingfisher?

350
00:22:07,607 --> 00:22:09,523
Because it's not his style.

351
00:22:09,523 --> 00:22:12,092
Even killers have a style?

352
00:22:13,803 --> 00:22:17,427
Professionally, we call it a "pattern."

353
00:22:17,427 --> 00:22:19,463
A pattern...

354
00:22:19,463 --> 00:22:22,531
Well, the targets have changed.

355
00:22:22,531 --> 00:22:23,799
That's why no message this time.

356
00:22:23,799 --> 00:22:26,403
He copied the method,
but something about it feels different.

357
00:22:26,403 --> 00:22:29,092
So you were thinking the same thing as me?

358
00:22:30,775 --> 00:22:32,903
I never said that.

359
00:22:32,903 --> 00:22:35,127
Your face did.

360
00:22:35,127 --> 00:22:38,892
I'm pretty good at reading people.

361
00:22:42,055 --> 00:22:46,692
Well, sounds like you two
are on the same page.

362
00:22:46,692 --> 00:22:51,339
Now that you're done,
can I make a bombshell announcement?

363
00:22:51,339 --> 00:22:53,863
- A bombshell...
- Announcement?

364
00:22:53,863 --> 00:22:55,563
I'm...

365
00:22:57,219 --> 00:22:58,792
going to become a cop.

366
00:22:58,792 --> 00:23:01,159
I'm going to become a cop.

367
00:23:01,159 --> 00:23:02,231
- What?
- What did you say?

368
00:23:02,231 --> 00:23:05,923
I'm going to become a cop
and catch all the...

369
00:23:05,923 --> 00:23:07,615
- bad guys.
- Wait, why of all things...

370
00:23:07,615 --> 00:23:09,359
Seriously? Awesome!

371
00:23:10,907 --> 00:23:12,272
Is that something to be happy about?

372
00:23:12,272 --> 00:23:14,441
- Then should I try to stop her?
- Of course!

373
00:23:14,441 --> 00:23:16,331
- Why?
- Well...

374
00:23:16,331 --> 00:23:18,807
Because being a cop is dangerous.

375
00:23:18,807 --> 00:23:20,426
Who? The criminals?

376
00:23:20,426 --> 00:23:23,339
And she'd have to study for years
just to pass the exam.

377
00:23:23,339 --> 00:23:25,339
Oh, there's also a special recruitment
program for martial artists.

378
00:23:25,339 --> 00:23:27,183
Really? They have that?

379
00:23:27,183 --> 00:23:28,423
- Look, Se Ah.
- Yes.

380
00:23:28,423 --> 00:23:29,526
- What?
- If you look around,

381
00:23:29,526 --> 00:23:31,427
- you could find...
- I'm rooting for you, Kwon Se Dol!

382
00:23:31,427 --> 00:23:33,063
You know I'll be your senior
if you become a cop, right?

383
00:23:33,063 --> 00:23:34,291
Oh, shut up!

384
00:23:34,291 --> 00:23:36,792
Special recruitment for martial artists?
How does that work?

385
00:23:36,792 --> 00:23:40,175
Here's how you do it.
Well, the competition's pretty stiff.

386
00:23:40,175 --> 00:23:42,595
Having a medal from an international
competition would give you an advantage.

387
00:23:42,595 --> 00:23:43,768
- You don't have one.
- No, but I've won

388
00:23:43,768 --> 00:23:44,792
plenty of domestic competitions.

389
00:23:44,792 --> 00:23:46,205
Really? Then your next shot would be

390
00:23:46,205 --> 00:23:47,859
the Commissioner General's Cup competition...

391
00:23:51,645 --> 00:23:53,863
Oh, this is nice.

392
00:23:56,655 --> 00:23:59,324
What made you make such a drastic decision?

393
00:24:00,063 --> 00:24:01,859
Was it because of your friend?

394
00:24:01,859 --> 00:24:05,759
Oh, well, he did have some influence.

395
00:24:05,759 --> 00:24:11,211
But more than that, I think
being a police officer is a great job.

396
00:24:11,211 --> 00:24:13,959
But why all of a sudden...

397
00:24:15,207 --> 00:24:19,975
It felt like my heart was racing.

398
00:24:19,975 --> 00:24:23,303
When I caught those attackers last time.

399
00:24:23,303 --> 00:24:27,359
And when I caught that
voice phishing scammer recently.

400
00:24:29,895 --> 00:24:35,259
The other day, Assistant Manager Ki,
when you told me you loved me.

401
00:24:35,259 --> 00:24:36,259
Back then, I...

402
00:24:36,259 --> 00:24:38,492
Oh, I know.

403
00:24:38,492 --> 00:24:41,126
You didn't mean anything by it.
You were just saying it casually.

404
00:24:41,126 --> 00:24:46,947
Who'd seriously say that to a woman
they've only met a few times?

405
00:24:46,947 --> 00:24:50,659
That night, I happened to run into Seong Hun.

406
00:24:50,659 --> 00:24:52,553
I asked him to go to a PC bang with me,

407
00:24:52,553 --> 00:24:55,683
but he said he had work
the next day and left.

408
00:24:55,683 --> 00:24:59,815
At first, I found him a bit annoying,
but then it suddenly hit me...

409
00:24:59,815 --> 00:25:02,987
"Oh, I'm this old,

410
00:25:02,987 --> 00:25:07,263
but I don't even
have a job to go to, no career,

411
00:25:07,263 --> 00:25:10,611
and I'm not pulling my weight in society."

412
00:25:10,611 --> 00:25:13,159
Aren't you in grad school?

413
00:25:13,995 --> 00:25:17,647
I just went to grad school
because it was related to my major.

414
00:25:17,647 --> 00:25:20,959
I was wondering
what I should do with my life,

415
00:25:20,959 --> 00:25:24,687
and then I remembered that moment.

416
00:25:24,687 --> 00:25:31,526
How my heart raced
when I caught those bad guys.

417
00:25:33,227 --> 00:25:38,727
I'm not particularly good at anything,
and judo is all I really have.

418
00:25:38,727 --> 00:25:40,447
But if I keep using it,

419
00:25:40,447 --> 00:25:45,926
maybe I can help
make the world a little better?

420
00:25:47,337 --> 00:25:53,075
Se Ah, do you believe the law
and the police can protect everyone?

421
00:25:53,075 --> 00:25:57,019
Unless you're the police,
you can't catch criminals.

422
00:25:57,019 --> 00:25:59,447
And there's no other way
to punish them by law, right?

423
00:25:59,447 --> 00:26:01,247
What if there were another way?

424
00:26:01,247 --> 00:26:04,709
- What?
- Maybe somewhere in this world,

425
00:26:04,709 --> 00:26:07,419
there are people who do that
in a different way.

426
00:26:07,419 --> 00:26:11,076
With the same goal of
making the world a better place,

427
00:26:11,076 --> 00:26:14,171
protecting the people
the police fail to protect,

428
00:26:14,171 --> 00:26:17,259
and punishing those who escape punishment

429
00:26:19,656 --> 00:26:21,356
under the law.

430
00:26:47,266 --> 00:26:53,092
<i>Someone who can imitate Kingfisher
and wants to bring you down?</i>

431
00:27:09,781 --> 00:27:12,711
Yul is finally asleep.
I read her two whole books.

432
00:27:12,711 --> 00:27:15,459
No wonder. I thought you dozed off with her.

433
00:27:15,459 --> 00:27:18,683
Honey, once we finish this,
we're done for the day.

434
00:27:18,683 --> 00:27:21,459
Then shall we have something cold to drink?

435
00:27:22,733 --> 00:27:24,883
How about a beer?

436
00:27:24,883 --> 00:27:26,592
- Beer?
- Yeah.

437
00:27:29,119 --> 00:27:33,375
I heard a beer after putting the kids to bed
tastes like heaven.

438
00:27:33,375 --> 00:27:35,159
- Putting the kids to bed?
- Yeah.

439
00:27:35,922 --> 00:27:36,951
Clocking out of parenting?

440
00:27:36,951 --> 00:27:41,651
So this is what they say washes away
all the day's stress and exhaustion.

441
00:27:41,651 --> 00:27:43,692
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

442
00:27:45,726 --> 00:27:47,726
Oh, that's refreshing.

443
00:27:48,975 --> 00:27:52,759
Oh, it feels like all that
pent-up stress just melts away.

444
00:27:56,992 --> 00:27:59,826
Now I see why people love drinking this.

445
00:28:01,635 --> 00:28:05,892
But you know what? Yul seems
really fascinated by her first plane ride.

446
00:28:05,892 --> 00:28:07,735
She's been talking about it all day.

447
00:28:07,735 --> 00:28:10,179
"Mommy, we flew through the sky, right?"

448
00:28:10,179 --> 00:28:13,151
"The fluffy clouds were
so pretty, weren't they?"

449
00:28:13,151 --> 00:28:15,826
"And we saw the ocean
from up in the sky, too, right?"

450
00:28:15,826 --> 00:28:19,095
Luckily, she wasn't scared of flying at all.

451
00:28:19,095 --> 00:28:21,267
We'll have to take her
on another flight soon.

452
00:28:21,267 --> 00:28:25,687
Yul is pretty... active, you know?

453
00:28:25,687 --> 00:28:26,959
And she's not easily scared.

454
00:28:26,959 --> 00:28:30,623
Maybe she should try something
a little more active, don't you think?

455
00:28:30,623 --> 00:28:32,359
For example, like...

456
00:28:33,795 --> 00:28:35,459
swimming,

457
00:28:36,467 --> 00:28:39,154
taekwondo, or skiing?

458
00:28:39,154 --> 00:28:42,092
Is snowboarding a little wilder than skiing?

459
00:28:42,092 --> 00:28:44,159
She likes scary things.

460
00:28:44,159 --> 00:28:46,326
- What about you?
- Huh?

461
00:28:48,295 --> 00:28:50,692
Don't you have anything you want to do?

462
00:28:52,555 --> 00:28:57,359
I've done everything
I wanted to try since I met you.

463
00:29:00,685 --> 00:29:03,579
Which one did you like best?

464
00:29:03,579 --> 00:29:05,859
I loved them all.

465
00:29:05,859 --> 00:29:07,559
I loved every moment.

466
00:29:10,499 --> 00:29:15,348
Walking hand in hand with you and chatting
as we walked through the flowers.

467
00:29:15,348 --> 00:29:18,526
And all those picnics by the Han River.

468
00:29:18,526 --> 00:29:23,031
And every Sunday, you being the chef
making black bean noodles?

469
00:29:23,031 --> 00:29:27,723
And all those late-night
horror movies you hated.

470
00:29:27,723 --> 00:29:30,751
All the pretty selfies we took together.

471
00:29:30,751 --> 00:29:32,451
All those things.

472
00:29:34,315 --> 00:29:37,326
Well, those are all such ordinary things.

473
00:29:38,059 --> 00:29:40,526
They're all special to me.

474
00:29:42,011 --> 00:29:45,526
There's still so much I want to do with you.

475
00:29:46,647 --> 00:29:48,347
Really?

476
00:29:49,371 --> 00:29:55,992
Something we haven't done before.
Something better and more special.

477
00:29:56,619 --> 00:30:00,823
Let's do every single one of them together.

478
00:30:01,831 --> 00:30:03,667
Yeah.

479
00:30:03,667 --> 00:30:05,459
Together.

480
00:30:08,855 --> 00:30:10,555
Shall we drink?

481
00:30:26,259 --> 00:30:28,692
[Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency]

482
00:30:38,475 --> 00:30:39,826
[Trace Evidence Analysis Report]
Mr. Lee, these are the analysis results

483
00:30:39,826 --> 00:30:41,726
for the trace evidence from the scenes.

484
00:30:43,175 --> 00:30:44,271
No way!

485
00:30:44,271 --> 00:30:45,599
Why? What is it?

486
00:30:45,599 --> 00:30:49,292
They found hair with matching DNA
at both sniper locations?

487
00:30:50,071 --> 00:30:52,819
- What?
- No match in the police database...

488
00:30:52,819 --> 00:30:55,119
But is there any basic profile?
What about the gender?

489
00:30:55,119 --> 00:30:56,667
Oh, here it is!

490
00:30:56,667 --> 00:30:59,926
Female, estimated to be in her 30s?

491
00:31:02,971 --> 00:31:04,923
Wow. What is this?

492
00:31:04,923 --> 00:31:06,623
[Female, Estimated 30s]
If it's a woman...

493
00:31:07,364 --> 00:31:10,159
Could it be the person that pickpocket saw?

494
00:31:13,407 --> 00:31:15,433
We entered the man's build, clothing,

495
00:31:15,433 --> 00:31:16,679
and wheelchair details
into the search program

496
00:31:16,679 --> 00:31:19,483
and tracked his movements
on CCTV over several days.

497
00:31:19,483 --> 00:31:21,007
I found something unusual.

498
00:31:21,007 --> 00:31:22,707
What is it?

499
00:31:23,471 --> 00:31:28,092
He kept going around this area,
so I tracked his movements.

500
00:31:29,311 --> 00:31:31,359
This is what I found.

501
00:31:32,567 --> 00:31:35,595
He went onto that island
and circled its perimeter several times.

502
00:31:35,595 --> 00:31:37,723
I think it might be some kind of message.

503
00:31:37,723 --> 00:31:40,663
The bottom looks like a crescent moon.

504
00:31:40,663 --> 00:31:44,855
The top is the eye,
and the bottom is the eyebrow?

505
00:31:44,855 --> 00:31:46,447
Could it be something like that?

506
00:31:46,447 --> 00:31:49,855
The victims, the eyes.

507
00:31:50,895 --> 00:31:52,747
Oh, you're right.

508
00:31:52,747 --> 00:31:57,327
Both victims were shot in the eye
this time, weren't they?

509
00:31:57,327 --> 00:32:02,711
According to our internal police network,
could this be connected to the case?

510
00:32:02,711 --> 00:32:05,692
The vital spot of every beast

511
00:32:06,515 --> 00:32:08,215
is the eye.

512
00:32:14,883 --> 00:32:20,692
Someone who can imitate Kingfisher
and wants to bring you down?

513
00:32:22,167 --> 00:32:24,883
How long will it take
to trace a restricted number?

514
00:32:24,883 --> 00:32:26,708
If the original number
is still recorded in the network,

515
00:32:26,708 --> 00:32:28,295
it could take as little as 15 minutes.

516
00:32:28,295 --> 00:32:30,226
I need it within ten minutes.

517
00:32:32,019 --> 00:32:33,792
Sooner if possible.

518
00:32:44,831 --> 00:32:46,559
Where are you now?

519
00:33:01,926 --> 00:33:06,792
[Summer 2008, Russia]

520
00:33:19,535 --> 00:33:20,707
The boss is having dinner.

521
00:33:20,707 --> 00:33:22,463
He's having a late dinner, huh?

522
00:33:22,463 --> 00:33:27,011
How can a punk who slaughtered
an entire family stomach his food?

523
00:33:27,011 --> 00:33:29,007
It's a waste of good food.

524
00:33:29,007 --> 00:33:30,559
Let's finish this and go.

525
00:33:30,559 --> 00:33:33,379
Even death row inmates get a last meal.

526
00:33:33,379 --> 00:33:34,567
Just wait.

527
00:33:34,567 --> 00:33:38,292
That's your problem.

528
00:33:39,135 --> 00:33:41,959
If it's too much trouble, I can do it.

529
00:33:42,631 --> 00:33:46,159
A punk like that deserves
a bullet right in the eye...

530
00:33:52,967 --> 00:33:54,691
Haven't seen that before.

531
00:33:54,691 --> 00:33:57,007
Oh, this?

532
00:33:57,007 --> 00:33:59,703
I liked it, so I got one tattooed.

533
00:33:59,703 --> 00:34:01,663
It's just like that saying.

534
00:34:01,663 --> 00:34:04,675
The vital spot of every beast

535
00:34:04,675 --> 00:34:05,919
is the eye.

536
00:34:05,919 --> 00:34:08,459
How is it? Pretty awesome, right?

537
00:34:09,399 --> 00:34:11,326
Keep an eye on the surroundings.

538
00:34:12,226 --> 00:34:13,316
Dinner's over.

539
00:34:13,316 --> 00:34:15,016
He's leaving.

540
00:34:27,951 --> 00:34:29,155
Mission accomplished.

541
00:34:29,155 --> 00:34:30,899
Good work.

542
00:34:30,899 --> 00:34:32,599
Clean up and come back.

543
00:34:42,692 --> 00:34:45,792
Oh, dear. We have a witness.

544
00:34:45,792 --> 00:34:46,826
You must be the boss's daughter.

545
00:34:46,826 --> 00:34:48,926
Layla, wait, let me handle...

546
00:34:58,655 --> 00:35:00,615
Are you insane?

547
00:35:00,615 --> 00:35:02,119
Do you have any idea what you've done?

548
00:35:02,119 --> 00:35:04,651
What? Shot a kid?

549
00:35:04,651 --> 00:35:06,526
Or shot her in the eye?

550
00:35:10,451 --> 00:35:13,839
"Eliminate any witnesses immediately."

551
00:35:13,839 --> 00:35:15,731
I was just following orders.

552
00:35:15,731 --> 00:35:19,259
Isn't the eye a witness's vital spot?

553
00:35:19,931 --> 00:35:22,892
Who on earth gave that kind of order?

554
00:35:23,947 --> 00:35:28,899
"Your name, in death,
only ends up on your tombstone."

555
00:35:28,899 --> 00:35:34,159
"But your sins, even in death,
are passed down to your children."

556
00:35:40,911 --> 00:35:42,492
She was just a child.

557
00:35:42,492 --> 00:35:45,271
She had no weapon and didn't even scream.

558
00:35:45,271 --> 00:35:47,907
She was just a scared little girl.

559
00:35:47,907 --> 00:35:50,419
I heard she was his daughter.

560
00:35:50,419 --> 00:35:52,067
The child was innocent.

561
00:35:52,067 --> 00:35:56,659
Her dad killed countless innocent people.

562
00:35:56,659 --> 00:35:58,326
Some of them were children too.

563
00:35:58,326 --> 00:36:00,692
You used to say it all the time.

564
00:36:00,692 --> 00:36:03,587
I thought you just meant it as a warning.

565
00:36:03,587 --> 00:36:05,591
We've never done anything like this.

566
00:36:05,591 --> 00:36:07,807
Because we'd never been caught.

567
00:36:07,807 --> 00:36:11,403
A witness eventually becomes a voice.

568
00:36:11,403 --> 00:36:13,826
And that voice calls for revenge.

569
00:36:17,043 --> 00:36:19,326
You could've been killed.

570
00:36:21,543 --> 00:36:24,539
Then you should've killed me instead.

571
00:36:24,539 --> 00:36:27,339
"Those children are safe now."

572
00:36:27,339 --> 00:36:29,959
"You saved them."

573
00:36:29,959 --> 00:36:34,515
You said that to me when I was eight.

574
00:36:34,515 --> 00:36:36,611
- I did.
- I don't recall anywhere

575
00:36:36,611 --> 00:36:40,899
in those words saying it's okay
to kill innocent people to save someone.

576
00:36:40,899 --> 00:36:42,599
Is that so?

577
00:36:46,559 --> 00:36:51,339
Today, we broke the most important rule
we're supposed to uphold.

578
00:36:51,339 --> 00:36:53,792
You don't see it the way I do, Mama.

579
00:36:54,443 --> 00:36:56,143
Am I right?

580
00:36:58,635 --> 00:37:00,335
So?

581
00:37:03,619 --> 00:37:08,335
Thank you for raising me
and teaching me all these years.

582
00:37:08,335 --> 00:37:11,626
I thought I'd get the chance
to repay you someday.

583
00:37:17,655 --> 00:37:19,359
Take care of yourself.

584
00:37:29,547 --> 00:37:31,826
You tracked me down faster than I thought.

585
00:37:32,679 --> 00:37:34,959
You already knew.

586
00:37:34,959 --> 00:37:37,659
That's why you came to Korea.

587
00:37:39,767 --> 00:37:41,611
Are you helping her?

588
00:37:41,611 --> 00:37:43,526
Or hunting her?

589
00:37:45,703 --> 00:37:48,259
Losing her every single time?

590
00:37:49,743 --> 00:37:52,526
Seoul is bigger than I thought, isn't it?

591
00:37:53,799 --> 00:37:55,895
What's the reason?

592
00:37:55,895 --> 00:37:58,735
The reason Layla's doing this to me.

593
00:37:58,735 --> 00:38:01,759
In short? Or the long version?

594
00:38:03,231 --> 00:38:05,192
The short version?

595
00:38:08,251 --> 00:38:10,392
Well, resentment toward you?

596
00:38:14,571 --> 00:38:16,426
What do you mean?

597
00:38:17,031 --> 00:38:18,223
Why would she resent me?

598
00:38:18,223 --> 00:38:20,159
Unintentionally,

599
00:38:20,771 --> 00:38:23,026
I happened to see something.

600
00:38:24,227 --> 00:38:26,417
<i>When I heard you two were working together,</i>

601
00:38:26,417 --> 00:38:30,992
<i>I got curious and followed you that day
without you knowing.</i>

602
00:38:34,351 --> 00:38:39,111
<i>She clearly saw that girl,
but why hasn't she told you?</i>

603
00:38:39,111 --> 00:38:41,707
- Mission accomplished.
- Good work.

604
00:38:41,707 --> 00:38:43,407
Clean up and come back.

605
00:38:47,871 --> 00:38:50,379
Oh, dear. We have a witness.

606
00:38:50,379 --> 00:38:53,126
- You must be the boss's daughter.
- Layla, wait, let me handle...

607
00:38:55,515 --> 00:38:57,392
<i>I realized in that moment.</i>

608
00:38:57,392 --> 00:38:59,163
<i>That girl was nothing</i>

609
00:38:59,163 --> 00:39:02,492
- <i>but prey caught in Layla's trap.</i>
- Are you insane?

610
00:39:02,492 --> 00:39:05,223
<i>Layla deliberately let that girl see you.</i>

611
00:39:05,223 --> 00:39:06,923
Take care of yourself.

612
00:39:22,247 --> 00:39:26,927
If you're going to look like you just
lost an arm, you should've stopped her.

613
00:39:26,927 --> 00:39:30,711
She started this life
by her own will and choice.

614
00:39:30,711 --> 00:39:34,459
I promised she could leave
whenever she wanted.

615
00:39:38,399 --> 00:39:40,795
Why didn't you tell her?

616
00:39:40,795 --> 00:39:43,126
That you never gave the order?

617
00:39:44,411 --> 00:39:45,926
Because I wasn't sure.

618
00:39:45,926 --> 00:39:49,531
Because I wasn't sure I could give

619
00:39:49,531 --> 00:39:55,203
the same order
if a witness actually appeared.

620
00:39:55,203 --> 00:39:58,231
A mentor trying to protect her disciple,

621
00:39:58,231 --> 00:40:02,059
and a disciple who'd rather die herself.

622
00:40:04,343 --> 00:40:06,559
It wouldn't have lasted much longer anyway.

623
00:40:08,571 --> 00:40:12,692
Sometimes, she was my mentor too.

624
00:40:14,371 --> 00:40:16,326
Take care of her from now on.

625
00:40:18,131 --> 00:40:19,691
Take care of what?

626
00:40:19,691 --> 00:40:20,875
Yoo Bo Na.

627
00:40:20,875 --> 00:40:23,983
Where she goes, what she does,

628
00:40:23,983 --> 00:40:25,383
and whether she's safe.

629
00:40:25,383 --> 00:40:28,787
Layla was kicked out of
the organization over that.

630
00:40:28,787 --> 00:40:33,851
She moved to Southeast Asia and now
works as a hired killer, quite in demand.

631
00:40:33,851 --> 00:40:37,695
You know what that is, right?
Getting paid to kill people.

632
00:40:37,695 --> 00:40:41,759
Then we recently learned
she'd returned to Korea.

633
00:40:42,807 --> 00:40:44,927
Did Mama send you?

634
00:40:44,927 --> 00:40:47,735
Sorry for being so messed up all this time.

635
00:40:47,735 --> 00:40:51,543
My mom cherishes her disciple
more than her own son,

636
00:40:51,543 --> 00:40:54,451
so can't the son get a little salty about it?

637
00:40:54,451 --> 00:40:56,726
If Kingfisher was the first target,

638
00:40:58,256 --> 00:41:00,355
I must be next.

639
00:41:00,355 --> 00:41:02,459
Well,

640
00:41:02,459 --> 00:41:05,992
do you really think
I don't know what you know?

641
00:41:10,875 --> 00:41:12,792
Your Achilles' heels.

642
00:41:15,735 --> 00:41:18,475
Don't you ever think about coming back?

643
00:41:18,475 --> 00:41:20,035
Mama...

644
00:41:20,035 --> 00:41:22,459
I think she's still waiting for you.

645
00:41:25,211 --> 00:41:27,326
You said you sent her my info.

646
00:41:27,983 --> 00:41:29,955
She probably already knows.

647
00:41:29,955 --> 00:41:32,226
That I'm not coming back.

648
00:41:34,507 --> 00:41:36,292
Give her my regards.

649
00:41:41,395 --> 00:41:43,759
She must be very disappointed.

650
00:41:48,007 --> 00:41:49,675
Did you find her?

651
00:41:49,675 --> 00:41:51,755
No. I'll go myself.

652
00:41:51,755 --> 00:41:54,026
Send me the location.

653
00:42:22,291 --> 00:42:25,747
Ms. Hee Seon, yeah. You're with Yul, right?

654
00:42:25,747 --> 00:42:27,926
Oh, yeah. We just left the daycare.

655
00:42:27,926 --> 00:42:29,375
Did anything seem strange?

656
00:42:29,375 --> 00:42:31,771
Like anyone suspicious hanging around.

657
00:42:31,771 --> 00:42:34,183
No, not at all. Why? Why do you ask?

658
00:42:34,183 --> 00:42:35,587
Oh, it's nothing.

659
00:42:35,587 --> 00:42:39,663
Could you go straight home?
I'm coming to pick her up now.

660
00:42:39,663 --> 00:42:41,826
Okay. Let's go.

661
00:42:42,492 --> 00:42:44,526
[My Heart]

662
00:43:14,051 --> 00:43:16,023
Someone once asked me...

663
00:43:16,023 --> 00:43:17,635
<i>What if...</i>

664
00:43:17,635 --> 00:43:21,659
What would you do if you lost
the things that matter most to you?

665
00:43:23,023 --> 00:43:24,723
I don't know.

666
00:43:25,527 --> 00:43:27,592
I've never thought about it.

667
00:43:28,843 --> 00:43:30,411
Because I don't believe
that will ever happen.

668
00:43:30,411 --> 00:43:35,159
Actually, I sometimes imagine
a life without Tae Seong.

669
00:43:36,619 --> 00:43:40,259
And every time, I can't picture anything.

670
00:43:40,879 --> 00:43:43,159
Just like...

671
00:43:43,159 --> 00:43:45,526
my heart has stopped.

672
00:43:46,211 --> 00:43:47,659
<i>Life without Tae Seong...</i>

673
00:43:47,659 --> 00:43:48,759
[My Heart]

674
00:43:48,759 --> 00:43:51,923
<i>would be like death, right?</i>

675
00:43:51,923 --> 00:43:53,426
<i>Because I love him.</i>

676
00:43:53,426 --> 00:43:54,667
[Big Precious]

677
00:43:54,667 --> 00:43:56,726
<i>Because I love him so much.</i>

678
00:43:56,726 --> 00:43:58,759
[My Heart]

679
00:44:07,556 --> 00:44:08,915
How long has he been inside?

680
00:44:08,915 --> 00:44:11,135
He went in five minutes ago.
He hasn't come out yet.

681
00:44:11,135 --> 00:44:12,835
Really?

682
00:44:27,823 --> 00:44:30,299
Darn it, this punk...

683
00:44:30,299 --> 00:44:32,026
He walked right out.

684
00:44:36,759 --> 00:44:39,726
[Not Today]

685
00:44:39,726 --> 00:44:41,275
[Team Leader Bong]

686
00:44:41,275 --> 00:44:42,467
Yes, Team Leader.

687
00:44:42,467 --> 00:44:45,075
We lost him. The wheelchair was a fake.

688
00:44:45,075 --> 00:44:46,775
What?

689
00:45:21,519 --> 00:45:23,339
Tae Seong!

690
00:45:23,339 --> 00:45:25,841
Honey, what brings you here?

691
00:45:25,841 --> 00:45:27,248
Why weren't you answering your phone?

692
00:45:27,248 --> 00:45:28,766
- I called you several times.
- My phone?

693
00:45:28,766 --> 00:45:31,959
I must've left it at the office.
Sorry, but what's up? Is something wrong?

694
00:45:31,959 --> 00:45:33,895
No, nothing's wrong.

695
00:45:33,895 --> 00:45:36,599
Well, actually... It's just that, honey.

696
00:45:36,599 --> 00:45:40,526
Someone I know said they were sending me
a package, so I gave them an address.

697
00:45:40,526 --> 00:45:43,447
Then I realized I'd stupidly
given them your office address.

698
00:45:43,447 --> 00:45:44,839
You did?

699
00:45:44,839 --> 00:45:47,126
So I called you a few times,
but you didn't answer.

700
00:45:47,126 --> 00:45:49,777
So I was passing by and thought
I'd stop in and see you.

701
00:45:49,777 --> 00:45:51,423
- Sorry to bother you while you're busy.
- No, it's fine.

702
00:45:51,423 --> 00:45:52,467
You came out to get it?

703
00:45:52,467 --> 00:45:54,371
Of course, I did. It's totally fine.

704
00:45:54,371 --> 00:45:55,955
- Sorry.
- It's fine. Don't worry.

705
00:45:55,955 --> 00:45:58,437
- I should get back to work.
- Okay.

706
00:45:58,437 --> 00:46:00,526
- Take care.
- Bye!

707
00:46:04,295 --> 00:46:05,326
- Honey.
- Yeah?

708
00:46:05,326 --> 00:46:07,259
Why does it feel so hard to leave?

709
00:46:07,863 --> 00:46:09,323
Are you working late tonight?

710
00:46:09,323 --> 00:46:10,821
I have some outside work,
but it should end early.

711
00:46:10,821 --> 00:46:12,492
I'll come home early.

712
00:46:13,803 --> 00:46:17,592
Okay. See you at home.
I really should go, as much as I hate to.

713
00:47:09,155 --> 00:47:13,695
<i>Your name, in death,
only ends up on your tombstone.</i>

714
00:47:13,695 --> 00:47:19,055
<i>But your sins, even in death,
are passed down to your children.</i>

715
00:47:19,055 --> 00:47:21,226
<i>Layla, wait, let me handle...</i>

716
00:47:26,459 --> 00:47:29,531
[Ms. Hee Seon]

717
00:47:29,531 --> 00:47:31,926
Yeah, Ms. Hee Seon, are you home now?

718
00:47:31,926 --> 00:47:33,511
You're with Yul, right?

719
00:47:33,511 --> 00:47:35,339
Bo Na, I can't find Yul anywhere!

720
00:47:35,339 --> 00:47:37,151
<i>What should I do?</i>

721
00:47:37,151 --> 00:47:38,335
As reported earlier,

722
00:47:38,335 --> 00:47:41,843
hair with matching DNA was found
at both sniper locations.

723
00:47:41,843 --> 00:47:46,559
The NFS analysis indicates
it belongs to a woman in her 30s.

724
00:47:57,779 --> 00:47:59,831
Please zoom in there.

725
00:47:59,831 --> 00:48:01,347
<i>Accordingly, we narrowed the suspect pool</i>

726
00:48:01,347 --> 00:48:02,947
[Suspect Pool Narrowed Down]
to women in their 30s.

727
00:48:02,947 --> 00:48:07,263
After rechecking CCTV and dashcam footage
collected around the crime scenes,

728
00:48:07,263 --> 00:48:11,359
we found one woman
who was present at both scenes.

729
00:48:11,359 --> 00:48:12,807
Is she really the same person?

730
00:48:12,807 --> 00:48:15,159
Her clothes and shoes are all different.

731
00:48:19,935 --> 00:48:24,507
As you can see, she has
the same tattoo in the same spot.

732
00:48:24,507 --> 00:48:27,187
A crescent moon below and an eye above.

733
00:48:27,187 --> 00:48:31,526
As you know, both victims
were shot in the eye.

734
00:48:32,543 --> 00:48:36,075
A dashcam from a car parked near
the second crime scene captured this woman

735
00:48:36,075 --> 00:48:38,992
[A Woman Gets in a Car and Drives Off]
getting into a car and driving off.

736
00:48:38,992 --> 00:48:40,583
[Zoom in on License Plate]
We ran the plate,

737
00:48:40,583 --> 00:48:41,942
[Owner: A Man in His 70s]
and the owner turned out to be a man

738
00:48:41,942 --> 00:48:43,371
[Who Died Three Years Ago]
in his 70s who died three years ago.

739
00:48:43,371 --> 00:48:45,155
So it's a stolen-identity car.

740
00:48:45,155 --> 00:48:46,299
Well, that's undeniable proof.

741
00:48:46,299 --> 00:48:48,011
[Seoul Traffic Control Center]
<i>We're using every available resource</i>

742
00:48:48,011 --> 00:48:50,147
<i>to track down the vehicle,
including the AI-powered integrated system</i>

743
00:48:50,147 --> 00:48:53,243
<i>for searching wanted vehicles
and intelligent CCTV systems</i>

744
00:48:53,243 --> 00:48:55,759
<i>operated by local governments.</i>

745
00:49:07,678 --> 00:49:09,378
Ugh.

746
00:49:13,675 --> 00:49:16,492
<i>It's been delivered.</i>

747
00:49:39,783 --> 00:49:41,187
Please spare me.

748
00:49:41,187 --> 00:49:43,091
Please, spare my life.

749
00:49:43,091 --> 00:49:47,595
If you want to live,
tell me what I want to hear.

750
00:49:47,595 --> 00:49:50,063
Oh... I really don't know anything.

751
00:49:50,063 --> 00:49:53,559
I've never even seen them.
I just did what I was paid to do.

752
00:49:56,715 --> 00:49:58,415
Unlock it.

753
00:50:19,667 --> 00:50:21,459
- Please let me see it.
- You can't.

754
00:50:21,459 --> 00:50:22,819
Bo Na, you're here?

755
00:50:22,819 --> 00:50:24,963
The kids wanted some, so we came.

756
00:50:24,963 --> 00:50:26,443
And while I was paying for a second...

757
00:50:26,443 --> 00:50:27,626
I asked to see the CCTV inside,

758
00:50:27,626 --> 00:50:28,971
[Authorized Personnel Only]
but they said no.

759
00:50:28,971 --> 00:50:32,603
Well, I told you I can't
just show it to anyone.

760
00:50:32,603 --> 00:50:35,247
If it's that important, bring the police.

761
00:50:35,247 --> 00:50:36,755
Excuse me.

762
00:50:36,755 --> 00:50:38,455
Hey!

763
00:50:43,695 --> 00:50:45,479
Oh, my. Who is that woman?

764
00:50:45,479 --> 00:50:48,292
Bo Na, do you know her?

765
00:51:01,371 --> 00:51:07,011
<i>Lately, I sometimes sense
something strange around me.</i>

766
00:51:07,011 --> 00:51:12,726
<i>Every time, every cell in
my body goes on high alert.</i>

767
00:51:13,567 --> 00:51:16,611
<i>I get this feeling that some danger</i>

768
00:51:16,611 --> 00:51:20,592
<i>stemming from me
could reach my child, my husband,</i>

769
00:51:21,363 --> 00:51:23,739
my family...

770
00:51:23,739 --> 00:51:25,459
Anxiety.

771
00:51:29,183 --> 00:51:33,526
<i>And every time, I pray with all my heart.</i>

772
00:51:34,483 --> 00:51:36,726
<i>If the blade cannot be stopped,</i>

773
00:51:37,363 --> 00:51:39,631
<i>let it come to me.</i>

774
00:51:39,631 --> 00:51:43,527
<i>Let the gun aim only at me.</i>

775
00:51:43,527 --> 00:51:45,227
Yul!

776
00:51:56,267 --> 00:51:58,126
Oh, Yul!

777
00:52:10,227 --> 00:52:11,479
Kwon Yul!

778
00:52:11,479 --> 00:52:12,783
Huh? Mommy!

779
00:52:12,783 --> 00:52:14,887
Lady, my mommy is here!

780
00:52:14,887 --> 00:52:16,895
Huh?

781
00:52:16,895 --> 00:52:18,883
Where did she go?

782
00:52:18,883 --> 00:52:20,491
Who?

783
00:52:20,491 --> 00:52:21,687
Yul, who was here?

784
00:52:21,687 --> 00:52:23,879
- Huh?
- Yeah, your friend.

785
00:52:23,879 --> 00:52:25,007
My friend?

786
00:52:25,007 --> 00:52:28,103
Yeah. She was pushing me
on the swing just now.

787
00:52:28,103 --> 00:52:30,059
But where did she go?

788
00:52:40,111 --> 00:52:44,259
Yul, I told you not
to follow strangers, remember?

789
00:52:44,259 --> 00:52:47,211
How could you come here alone
without telling Ms. Hee Seon?

790
00:52:47,211 --> 00:52:50,083
She's not a stranger. She's your friend.

791
00:52:50,083 --> 00:52:52,092
How do you know she's my friend?

792
00:52:52,092 --> 00:52:54,223
I've never shown you my friends.

793
00:52:54,223 --> 00:52:56,803
She showed me a photo of you two.

794
00:52:56,803 --> 00:52:58,503
A picture?

795
00:52:59,983 --> 00:53:02,026
Mommy, see? It's her.

796
00:53:06,379 --> 00:53:11,075
<i>"The vital spot of every beast is the eye."</i>

797
00:53:11,075 --> 00:53:12,995
<i>How is it? Pretty awesome, right?</i>

798
00:53:12,995 --> 00:53:17,147
<i>Enough playing around. Hurry over.</i>

799
00:53:17,147 --> 00:53:18,926
<i>I miss you.</i>

800
00:53:19,943 --> 00:53:22,195
As I mentioned on the phone,

801
00:53:22,195 --> 00:53:27,427
he was a teacher who was
respected his whole life.

802
00:53:27,427 --> 00:53:28,579
- I see.
- Yeah.

803
00:53:28,579 --> 00:53:33,459
Even now, his former students
still visit him on Teachers' Day.

804
00:53:38,835 --> 00:53:44,311
That was taken when he went to
Cambodia last summer.

805
00:53:44,311 --> 00:53:45,743
Cambodia?

806
00:53:45,743 --> 00:53:47,426
That's Angkor Wat in the background.

807
00:53:47,426 --> 00:53:50,623
It was one of his bucket-list trips.

808
00:53:50,623 --> 00:53:56,492
He went to Cambodia last year
and was planning to go to Bali this year.

809
00:54:02,183 --> 00:54:03,883
Hello.

810
00:54:05,359 --> 00:54:08,892
You remember me, right?
We met at the restaurant the other day.

811
00:54:09,707 --> 00:54:11,092
Oh, yes.

812
00:54:11,092 --> 00:54:16,059
It's just that you seemed to
have something to tell me that day.

813
00:54:16,059 --> 00:54:19,959
Could you tell me now, if that's okay?

814
00:54:27,426 --> 00:54:30,031
They came to the restaurant together.
Both of them.

815
00:54:30,031 --> 00:54:35,187
By both, you mean the doctor and...

816
00:54:35,187 --> 00:54:38,292
The middle school teacher who was shot first.

817
00:54:46,663 --> 00:54:48,915
Not just long-range.
Get me something for close range too.

818
00:54:48,915 --> 00:54:50,895
A suppressor, a knife, and a flashlight too.

819
00:54:50,895 --> 00:54:52,551
Hurry.

820
00:54:52,551 --> 00:54:54,619
Found it!

821
00:54:54,619 --> 00:54:58,747
The vehicle is currently
at the Yanghwa Han River Park parking lot.

822
00:54:58,747 --> 00:55:01,019
Finally!

823
00:55:01,019 --> 00:55:02,627
Get ready to move out.

824
00:55:02,627 --> 00:55:04,327
Yes, sir!

825
00:55:10,547 --> 00:55:12,603
Huh? Yul, Daddy's home!

826
00:55:12,603 --> 00:55:14,859
- I'm home.
- Daddy!

827
00:55:14,859 --> 00:55:17,292
Yul! There you are!

828
00:55:17,292 --> 00:55:18,595
You're home?

829
00:55:18,595 --> 00:55:20,523
What brings you here? Where is Bo Na?

830
00:55:20,523 --> 00:55:24,295
She had something urgent come up,
so she asked me to watch Yul.

831
00:55:24,295 --> 00:55:25,335
Something urgent? What happened?

832
00:55:25,335 --> 00:55:28,992
Well, I don't know either.
Must be something at work.

833
00:56:15,259 --> 00:56:17,459
Hi, my friend.

834
00:56:19,591 --> 00:56:21,119
Oh...

835
00:56:21,119 --> 00:56:24,107
Should I greet you the Korean way here?

836
00:56:24,107 --> 00:56:26,983
It's been a while, Yoo Bo Na.

837
00:56:26,983 --> 00:56:29,139
Why did you kill those people?

838
00:56:29,139 --> 00:56:31,067
What?

839
00:56:31,067 --> 00:56:34,639
That's the first thing you ask
before we've even caught up?

840
00:56:34,639 --> 00:56:38,959
Because I need to decide whether to kill you.

841
00:56:40,059 --> 00:56:41,627
Right.

842
00:56:41,627 --> 00:56:44,063
Our noble Kingfisher

843
00:56:44,063 --> 00:56:47,891
isn't the type to kill just anyone
over a bad mood.

844
00:56:47,891 --> 00:56:49,792
Should I wait longer?

845
00:56:50,459 --> 00:56:52,655
Sorry to disappoint you.

846
00:56:52,655 --> 00:56:55,092
That won't be enough to kill me.

847
00:56:57,727 --> 00:57:01,526
Did you know grilled bananas
taste like roasted sweet potatoes?

848
00:57:04,043 --> 00:57:06,415
There was a woman who always asked

849
00:57:06,415 --> 00:57:10,079
if I'd eaten whenever I came back from a job.

850
00:57:10,079 --> 00:57:12,807
She was a woman selling
cheap food on the street.

851
00:57:12,807 --> 00:57:15,826
No matter how often I ignored her,
she'd ask every day.

852
00:57:17,547 --> 00:57:19,526
"Have you eaten?"

853
00:57:20,191 --> 00:57:22,507
She wasn't afraid of anything.

854
00:57:22,507 --> 00:57:25,559
To someone who'd just
come back from killing someone...

855
00:57:27,107 --> 00:57:31,526
One day, I was hungry,
so I stopped and looked.

856
00:57:31,526 --> 00:57:35,959
She gathered up some food
and had her little daughter bring it to me.

857
00:57:37,411 --> 00:57:42,551
From then on, grilled bananas
from that woman became my dinner.

858
00:57:42,551 --> 00:57:44,692
One day, the mom and daughter

859
00:57:45,475 --> 00:57:49,051
were found dead in a pile of trash.

860
00:57:49,051 --> 00:57:53,492
It took me a while to find out who did it.

861
00:57:54,999 --> 00:57:58,126
I wondered whether to gouge out their eyes

862
00:57:58,126 --> 00:58:00,492
or tear them apart.

863
00:58:01,492 --> 00:58:06,027
While having fun pondering that,
I thought this way was pretty good too.

864
00:58:06,027 --> 00:58:10,359
Kill the ones who deserve it
and bring down Kingfisher too.

865
00:58:11,631 --> 00:58:13,331
Bang!

866
00:58:14,883 --> 00:58:17,699
Why are you doing this to me?

867
00:58:17,699 --> 00:58:20,603
I don't think I've done anything to you.

868
00:58:20,603 --> 00:58:22,326
Because you annoy me.

869
00:58:23,675 --> 00:58:27,426
Seeing you living like that
while I live like this,

870
00:58:28,219 --> 00:58:30,292
it makes my stomach churn.

871
00:58:34,392 --> 00:58:39,055
I killed that girl to protect Yoo Bo Na.

872
00:58:39,055 --> 00:58:43,292
I thought that's what you wanted,
Mama. Was I wrong?

873
00:58:44,087 --> 00:58:46,739
You should've killed Yoo Bo Na instead.

874
00:58:46,739 --> 00:58:48,439
What do you mean...

875
00:58:51,226 --> 00:58:56,571
Yoo Bo Na said,
"You should've killed me instead."

876
00:58:56,571 --> 00:58:58,359
Do you understand what that means?

877
00:59:00,587 --> 00:59:03,426
Not really.

878
00:59:04,611 --> 00:59:08,507
You don't know what Yoo Bo Na knows.

879
00:59:08,507 --> 00:59:10,675
That's why.

880
00:59:10,675 --> 00:59:12,459
That's why I'm casting you out.

881
00:59:12,459 --> 00:59:15,515
You're... kicking me out?

882
00:59:15,515 --> 00:59:16,871
Why?

883
00:59:16,871 --> 00:59:18,511
I... I...

884
00:59:18,511 --> 00:59:21,692
A girl who could kill without batting an eye.

885
00:59:21,692 --> 00:59:23,771
I was worried, but I kept watching.

886
00:59:23,771 --> 00:59:27,326
Sometimes, that nature
can be useful in the field.

887
00:59:27,326 --> 00:59:32,795
But you shouldn't have crossed the line.

888
00:59:32,795 --> 00:59:36,759
You shouldn't have proven
what kind of person you are.

889
00:59:36,759 --> 00:59:40,692
I wanted to be family.

890
00:59:41,931 --> 00:59:47,726
But no matter how hard I tried,
you only looked at Bo Na.

891
00:59:48,387 --> 00:59:50,647
How are we so different?

892
00:59:50,647 --> 00:59:52,859
She kills people, and so do I!

893
00:59:52,859 --> 00:59:54,943
It's just a fine line.

894
00:59:54,943 --> 00:59:57,243
Separated by a single fine line.

895
00:59:57,243 --> 01:00:02,087
How big a difference
that fine line makes will be proven

896
01:00:02,087 --> 01:00:05,526
by how your lives turn out.

897
01:00:06,247 --> 01:00:08,026
Don't you agree?

898
01:00:08,827 --> 01:00:12,623
<i>I should have killed you back then
instead of that girl.</i>

899
01:00:12,623 --> 01:00:16,851
That's how I was abandoned,
and this is how I live now.

900
01:00:16,851 --> 01:00:18,551
Thanks to you.

901
01:00:20,323 --> 01:00:22,023
No.

902
01:00:23,247 --> 01:00:26,292
You're the one who made you who you are.

903
01:00:28,179 --> 01:00:30,907
If you got what you wanted,
now go home quietly.

904
01:00:30,907 --> 01:00:32,943
While you're still alive.

905
01:00:32,943 --> 01:00:35,126
It's too late for that.

906
01:00:35,823 --> 01:00:39,726
I figured you'd be living
more or less like me.

907
01:00:40,371 --> 01:00:42,863
- <i>But...</i>
- Kingfisher,

908
01:00:42,863 --> 01:00:44,719
isn't he honestly amazing?

909
01:00:44,719 --> 01:00:46,083
He really is!

910
01:00:46,083 --> 01:00:47,883
The world needs someone like that.

911
01:00:47,883 --> 01:00:51,091
I wonder what he's like. I'm so curious.

912
01:00:51,091 --> 01:00:52,763
I'd love to meet him.

913
01:00:52,763 --> 01:00:56,391
<i>People here revere you like a hero?</i>

914
01:00:56,391 --> 01:01:00,626
While over there, everyone treats me
like a criminal punk.

915
01:01:02,195 --> 01:01:03,959
Mommy, are we staying the night?

916
01:01:03,959 --> 01:01:05,692
Yeah, we're staying one night.

917
01:01:05,692 --> 01:01:06,726
Yay!

918
01:01:06,726 --> 01:01:10,492
<i>You've got a loving husband,
a beautiful daughter, and...</i>

919
01:01:11,735 --> 01:01:13,895
<i>you even have a family.</i>

920
01:01:13,895 --> 01:01:16,626
<i>You even look pretty happy.</i>

921
01:01:23,007 --> 01:01:24,926
It's not fair.

922
01:01:26,431 --> 01:01:27,855
What we do...

923
01:01:27,855 --> 01:01:30,179
isn't all that different.

924
01:01:30,179 --> 01:01:31,879
You and I

925
01:01:32,711 --> 01:01:35,311
are going to hell when we die.

926
01:01:35,311 --> 01:01:37,692
The same hell?

927
01:01:38,483 --> 01:01:39,843
That sounds somewhat fair.

928
01:01:39,843 --> 01:01:42,126
I'll take my fair share of punishment.

929
01:01:42,915 --> 01:01:45,795
If there's punishment
I have to face while I'm alive,

930
01:01:45,795 --> 01:01:47,559
I'll take that too.

931
01:01:48,375 --> 01:01:50,075
But...

932
01:01:51,343 --> 01:01:53,126
leave my family out of this.

933
01:01:54,119 --> 01:01:56,259
I'm warning you.

934
01:01:56,259 --> 01:02:00,843
If you lay a finger on
my husband or my child,

935
01:02:00,843 --> 01:02:03,627
I'll make you experience hell
while you're still alive.

936
01:02:03,627 --> 01:02:05,711
Is that so?

937
01:02:05,711 --> 01:02:08,459
Then you can experience hell
while you're alive too.

938
01:02:09,719 --> 01:02:13,095
Get destroyed just like me.

939
01:02:13,095 --> 01:02:15,792
Forget everything you hold dear.

940
01:03:36,627 --> 01:03:39,507
Try killing me in front of your husband.

941
01:03:39,507 --> 01:03:41,326
It's you, Layla.

942
01:03:41,326 --> 01:03:42,326
Let's get her.

943
01:03:42,326 --> 01:03:44,579
The suspect must be taken alive.

944
01:03:44,579 --> 01:03:48,267
Yoo Bo Na, enjoy rotting in prison
for the rest of your life.

945
01:03:48,267 --> 01:03:50,203
Dong Jin's here. We have to go.

946
01:03:50,203 --> 01:03:51,583
We have to go. Hurry.

947
01:03:51,583 --> 01:03:54,287
I'll become your living hell.

948
01:03:54,287 --> 01:03:55,339
Ceasefire!

949
01:03:55,339 --> 01:03:59,492
Without you... how am I supposed to live?

950
01:04:00,992 --> 01:04:02,692
[Mommy, I miss you. I love you so much]

